# Subscriptions & Boost

## Trials are real subscriptions
A user "on free trial" is an **active store subscriber** (Apple/Google manage it;
`periodType = TRIAL`). The stores do **not** allow charging before a trial ends, so
never build a "pay early / skip the trial" flow on the subscription product, and never
show "already subscribed" as a dead-end to a trial user.

## Boost eligibility = active subscriber (paid OR trial) or admin
Boost is granted to the `premium` and `trial` DB tiers, plus admins. Free is denied.
This lives in **two mirrored modules — change both together**:
- Server: `artifacts/api-server/src/lib/boostEligibility.ts` (`BOOST_TIERS`,
  `userIsBoostEligible`) — used by `autoBoost.ts`.
- Client: `mobile/lib/serverSubscription.ts` (`subscriptionTierGrantsBoost`,
  `isServerBoostEligible`) — used by `revenuecat.tsx` `canUseBoost`.

`canUseBoost` also requires a confirmed store entitlement (not the optimistic
post-purchase flag) so it only lights up after the webhook syncs the DB tier.

```ts
// ✅ trial counts
const BOOST_TIERS = new Set(["premium", "trial"]);
// ❌ don't narrow boost back to paid-only — it traps trial subscribers
```

## Tier mapping is the webhook's job
`subscriptionFromEvent` maps store events → `premium | trial | free`. Don't infer tiers
elsewhere; read `user.subscription`.

## Only EXPIRATION revokes access
Access ends when the paid/trial period actually lapses, NOT when the user cancels.
- `EXPIRATION` → `free` (the only revoking event).
- `CANCELLATION` (auto-renew turned off) → **ignored** (no DB write). The user keeps
  access until `EXPIRATION` fires. Never downgrade here — it strips access already paid for.
- `BILLING_ISSUE` (e.g. insufficient funds) → **ignored**. The store opens a billing
  retry / grace window and the user keeps access; if it ultimately fails, `EXPIRATION`
  revokes. Surface a "fix your payment" nudge (client `rc.billingIssue` /
  `hasBillingIssue`), but never revoke server-side on this event.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — revokes access the user still has
const FREE_EVENTS = new Set(["CANCELLATION", "EXPIRATION", "BILLING_ISSUE"]);
// ✅ GOOD — only true lapse revokes
const FREE_EVENTS = new Set(["EXPIRATION"]);
```
